target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheBranchesNothingReached/a_hung_subprocess'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the budget is threaded through shTimeout into run.Run so the kill branch can be exercised in milliseconds. Passing the shBudget const instead makes that claim false by construction (a const cannot be lowered by a test), so the one branch deciding whether a hung gh fails open or closed has no test and cannot have one.
--- old
	rr := run.Run(repo, budget, prog, args...)
--- new
	rr := run.Run(repo, shBudget, prog, args...)
